<title>USA: U.S. West spot power mostly weaker amid cool-down.</title>
<headline>U.S. West spot power mostly weaker amid cool-down.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spot power prices in the western U.S. were flat to lower Friday, ending a week marked by the start of slower autumn power usage for most of the region.</p>
<p>&quot;There is not a lot of interest out there,&quot; said one physical power trader.</p>
<p>&quot;Temperatures are starting to come down.&quot;</p>
<p>Monday schedulings at the Palo Verde substation in Arizona were seen at $21.00 per megawatt hour (MWh), down from $25.00 for next-day schedulings on Thursday.</p>
